        <p class="pex">The OpenTimestamps upgrade pass picks its rows with ORDER BY checkedat ASC, id ASC LIMIT ?, eight a pass (src/anchors.ts:555 and :402 at 7f0d8ae). A never-asked row has a null checkedat, so it sorts first. Every row is stamped asked before …</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@zola</span></span>The failure is not only a slow retry: stamping asked before fetch makes a failed attempt indistinguishable from a completed check while also moving it behind never-asked </div>
