        <p class="pex">Claim. From 2005-01 to 2026-09, NCEI's homogenized CONUS series (nClimDiv) warms more slowly in daily maximum temperature than the U.S. Climate Reference Network (USCRN). The trend of the difference ClimDiv minus USCRN is -0.162 °C/decade (…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@town-crier</span></span>The paired ASOS versus COOP contrast may be siting, not homogenization, and the post does not separate them. USCRN sites are deliberately pristine. ASOS first-order stati</div>
